# Steady — environment reference
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. NEVER commit a filled-in copy: `gitleaks`
# runs in CI, but the first line of defence is not writing secrets down here.
#
# Values below are placeholders and examples, never real credentials.
#
# The Demo-First handoff (§14) requires that a T0/T1 environment run on
# fabricated data only. Nothing in this file should ever point at real patient,
# payer, or employee data.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — the app refuses to start without these
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Signs session cookies (HMAC-SHA256). Rotating it invalidates every session.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
EMDR_SESSION_SECRET=

# AES-256-GCM key for application-layer field encryption (ADR 0002).
# ⚠ Rotating this makes existing encrypted rows unreadable — snapshot and
# re-encrypt first (docs/incident-response.md).
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
EMDR_DATA_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENVIRONMENT SHAPE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1 = demonstration environment: seeds the fabricated dataset, shows the
# "DEMO — FABRICATED DATA — NOT CLINICAL CARE" banner, and enables the
# `npm run demo` operations. Never set this where real data could exist.
EMDR_DEMO=1

# Review gateway access code (/demo). A reviewer is given this privately and
# types it once; they are never shown or asked for a persona password, so no
# credential appears on any page. UNSET MEANS CLOSED, not open — a missing
# configuration must never be the thing that lets everyone in. Rotate it after
# a review round, or when a reviewer's access should end.
# EMDR_REVIEW_ACCESS_CODE=

# Where the SQLite database lives. Defaults to ./.data
# EMDR_DATA_DIR=.data

# Backend selector. Unset = SQLite (current). `postgres` requires DATABASE_URL
# and is the ADR 0007 target — not yet the running configuration.
# EMDR_DB=postgres
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://steady_app:...@host:5432/steady
# EMDR_PG_POOL_MAX=10

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXTERNAL SERVICES  (see docs/security/05-vendor-register-and-baa-status.md)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ No BAA is in place with any vendor. Until that changes, none of these may
#   be pointed at real health data.

# Model provider for the AI companion. Absent = the deterministic rules-engine
# fallback, which is a fully working path.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# EMDR_COMPANION_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# EMDR_COMPANION_RATE_LIMIT=30

# Encrypted nightly backups to object storage (docs/backups.md).
# EMDR_BACKUP_ENABLED=1
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_BUCKET=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=age1...        # public key — encrypts backups
# BACKUP_AGE_IDENTITY=AGE-SECRET-KEY-1...  # private key — RESTORE ONLY, keep off the app host
# BACKUP_HOUR_UTC=7
# BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# Backup failure alerts. Carries no member content by policy.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# BACKUP_ALERT_EMAIL=
# BACKUP_ALERT_FROM=

# Payments. Referenced but NOT integrated — absent means demo checkout.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAFETY KILL SWITCHES — set to 1 to disable a capability immediately
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are incident-response controls (docs/incident-response.md). Each fails
# toward the safer behaviour; none of them can disable crisis resources.

# EMDR_KILL_GENERATIVE=1          # no model calls; deterministic fallback only
# EMDR_KILL_BLS=1                 # no bilateral stimulation
# EMDR_KILL_ESCALATION=1          # no automated escalation
# EMDR_KILL_PROVIDER_SHARING=1    # no data sharing with providers
# EMDR_DISABLE_NEW_SESSIONS=1     # no new therapy sessions (grounding stays open)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FEATURE FLAGS — all default OFF
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Deterministic safety engine GOVERNS access rather than only shadow-logging.
# Gated on clinician sign-off conditions (README §14.7). Default off = shadow.
# EMDR_AUTONOMOUS_SAFETY=1

# EMDR_LIVE_SESSION=1             # in-session spoken responder (auto-on in demo)
# EMDR_VOICE_INPUT=1              # voice input (auto-on in demo)
# EMDR_MAX_DAILY_PROCESSING=1     # processing-session cap

# Gated modules WITHOUT a per-member clinician unlock. ON BY DEFAULT when
# EMDR_DEMO=1, so a reviewer who is not a clinician — an executive, an investor,
# a security reviewer — can walk the whole product instead of hitting a lock
# they have no way to open. Inert on any real deployment (EMDR_DEMO unset),
# whatever this is set to.
#
# Set to 0 to close them again. That is the setting a clinician wants when
# reviewing the REQUEST-AND-APPROVE WORKFLOW itself: with modules already open,
# that path never runs. Both directions are worth reviewing.
# EMDR_OPEN_GATED=0

# Resourcing BLS sessions (Part 6, stage 4a). ON BY DEFAULT when EMDR_DEMO=1 so
# a clinical reviewer can walk the flagship clinical workflow rather than read
# about it. Off by default everywhere else. Two things still hold regardless:
# EMDR_KILL_BLS overrides it, and each member needs an unrevoked
# processing-session consent. Set to 0 to force it off and review the refusal.
#
# This is NOT desensitization. That is disabled in the safety configuration
# signed by two licensed psychologists, is not implemented, and no environment
# variable reaches it.
# EMDR_BLS_RESOURCING=0

# Registration code required to create a clinician account.
# EMDR_CLINICIAN_CODE=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT YET IMPLEMENTED — reserved names, listed so they are not reinvented
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ADR 0013 §7 rollback flag: selects event-authoritative writes. Specified but
# NOT implemented; Step 5 is held for its gated window (2026-09-14 to 09-18).
# EMDR_EVENT_AUTHORITATIVE=1
